title lotus-audio — Lotus's insert_silence, the lossless twin of lotus-audio's shift, exact inverse of lotus-audio's cut
prompt recur the itinerary the Long Return Lila; after lotus-audio sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think lotus-audio (shift) slides the clip within a FIXED frame and DROPS what falls off — a lossy translation, honest that shift(k) then shift(-k) loses the dropped tail. Its true complement is not another way to translate but the gesture that OPENS rather than translates: insert silence. Every editor ships Insert -> Silence — open a gap of quiet so a downbeat lands where it should, so two takes align without overwriting either. Where shift keeps the length and loses samples, insert-silence keeps every sample and GROWS the length. Naming it beside shift teaches the one distinction about making room in a bounded signal: drop, or grow.
think Shape: insert_silence(clip, at, count) opens count silent seats at `at`, shifting the tail right high-index-first (exactly lotus-audio splice's own safe direction) and zero-filling the gap. It reuses timeline.EditError whole — BadRange when at > len, ClipFull when count > buf.len - len — each refused before any write, inventing no error of its own. One in-place pass bounded by len, no allocation, no second buffer.
think Four laws, all provable: the INSERT law (result is original[0..at] ++ zeros(count) ++ original[at..], length grown by count, checked at head/middle/tail); the INVERSE law (insert_silence(at,count) then lotus-audio's cut(at,count) returns the original byte for byte — the exact inverse of cut, the lossless round-trip the lossy shift honestly could not make, proven by importing timeline.cut just as lotus-audio imports lotus-audio's rotate); the PEAK / SILENCE law (the inserted span is all zero, so the peak re-measured through lotus-audio is UNCHANGED at any position — where shift's peak is non-increasing because it can drop a loud sample, insert-silence's is exactly preserved because it loses nothing); the DEGENERATE / REFUSAL law (count 0 the identity, at 0 the head, at = len the tail, an empty clip grown to pure silence, at > len BadRange, a count past the buffer ClipFull).
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — all four laws and both refusal branches, the clip verified untouched after each refused call so the refusal is proven to come before any write. The crux of correctness is reusing lotus-audio's proven pieces whole: splice's own high-index-first tail shift for the safe move, cut for the exact-inverse proof, EditError for the faults, meter for the peak. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged at 11); >=2 positive-invariant asserts per fn including the in-bounds guard on the tail-shift destination; width-check clean; no new arithmetic invented. Honest scope: the one thing insert_silence writes that was not already there is silence at the opened gap — no non-zero sample invented, nothing dropped.
loom witness=ales_insert_silence_witness green=1 laws=4 rung=lotus-audio
